⦃ ⧖ ⧖ ⧗̵¹ ⟗ ⧗̱⁰ ᚣᛊ ⧖ ⌁̵ ⧗̵⁰ ⦄ ⟨ ⟗ʃ ⟦ ℤ ⟧ ⊸ ◌ ⟦ ℤ ⟧ ⟩ ᚣᛋ ⸫

⍝ ==== s2 parser (spec §9, §18): token buffer → item tree, then tangle (§9.3)
The parser state is one array of ℤ after a sentinel. Slots 0 … 3 are ⍝
⍝ registers: position (in tokens), result (a node slot), start of the
tangled items, loop flag. Nodes follow in preorder: kind, token, size ⍝
⍝ (slots of the node and everything under it), fields, then children.
1 lit  2 call  3 anti-call  4 inverse-call  5 op         (leaves) ⍝
⍝ 6 shape-call: sig          7 quote: block     8 array: ops
9 block: ops               10 select: 3 faces 11 rselect: 3 faces, block ⍝
⍝ 12 face ⁼  13 face ∅       14 loop, 15 postselect, 16 prayer: block
17 handle: ok block, fail block ⍝
⍝ 20 sig [nin saw]: types    21 type [np prefix tokens…]: element type (⟦…⟧)
30 fragment [name rev ordinal hasSig]: body, sig ⍝
⍝ 31 particle [name]: type   32 ffi [name cname]: sig
40 fn [name rev nfr ordinals…]: sig, ops (after tangling) ⍝
⍝ Token slots point into the token buffer; −1 is the end of the file.

